{"version":1,"materials":{"g01":{"voice":"af_heart","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_heart（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"I get up at six every morning.":"materials/g01/01.mp3","First, I open the window and drink a glass of water.":"materials/g01/02.mp3","Then I make coffee and read the news on my phone.":"materials/g01/03.mp3","I like quiet mornings, because I can think about my day.":"materials/g01/04.mp3","At seven, I have breakfast with my family.":"materials/g01/05.mp3","We eat bread, eggs and fruit.":"materials/g01/06.mp3","After breakfast, I study English for ten minutes.":"materials/g01/07.mp3","I say new words out loud and try to remember them.":"materials/g01/08.mp3","At eight, I leave home and walk to the station.":"materials/g01/09.mp3","It takes about fifteen minutes.":"materials/g01/10.mp3","On the way, I listen to an English story.":"materials/g01/11.mp3","It is a good start to the day.":"materials/g01/12.mp3"}},"g02":{"voice":"am_michael","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_michael（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"Ken started a new job last month.":"materials/g02/01.mp3","He works for a small company that sells kitchen tools.":"materials/g02/02.mp3","On his first day, he was very nervous.":"materials/g02/03.mp3","He did not know anyone, and the office was big and busy.":"materials/g02/04.mp3","His manager, Ms. Brown, showed him around and introduced him to the team.":"materials/g02/05.mp3","Everyone was friendly.":"materials/g02/06.mp3","One woman, Lisa, helped him with the computer system.":"materials/g02/07.mp3","At lunch, they ate together and talked about their favorite food.":"materials/g02/08.mp3","Now Ken feels much better.":"materials/g02/09.mp3","He still makes some mistakes, but he is learning every day.":"materials/g02/10.mp3","He thinks the job is hard but interesting.":"materials/g02/11.mp3"}},"g03":{"voice":"bf_emma","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bf_emma（イギリス英語・女性）","clips":{"Yesterday it rained all day.":"materials/g03/01.mp3","In the evening, I took the train home.":"materials/g03/02.mp3","I was very tired, so I sat down and closed my eyes.":"materials/g03/03.mp3","When I got off the train, the rain had stopped.":"materials/g03/04.mp3","I walked home happily.":"materials/g03/05.mp3","At home, I suddenly remembered my umbrella.":"materials/g03/06.mp3","I had left it on the train!":"materials/g03/07.mp3","It was a blue umbrella, a present from my sister.":"materials/g03/08.mp3","This morning, I called the station.":"materials/g03/09.mp3","A kind man said, \"We have a blue umbrella.":"materials/g03/10.mp3","Please come and get it.\"":"materials/g03/11.mp3","I was so glad.":"materials/g03/12.mp3","Next time, I will hold my umbrella in my hand.":"materials/g03/13.mp3"}},"g04":{"voice":"bm_george","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bm_george（イギリス英語・男性）","clips":{"Mika and her friend Sam are talking about the weekend.":"materials/g04/01.mp3","Sam wants to go to the beach on Saturday.":"materials/g04/02.mp3","Mika likes the idea, but the weather report says it will be cold and windy.":"materials/g04/03.mp3","So they change the plan.":"materials/g04/04.mp3","On Saturday, they will visit a new museum in the city.":"materials/g04/05.mp3","It has a special show about space.":"materials/g04/06.mp3","On Sunday, Mika will stay home.":"materials/g04/07.mp3","She wants to clean her room and cook a big meal for her parents.":"materials/g04/08.mp3","Sam will play football with his team in the afternoon.":"materials/g04/09.mp3","They both feel that a good weekend needs some fun and some rest.":"materials/g04/10.mp3"}},"g05":{"voice":"af_bella","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_bella（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"\"Good morning.":"materials/g05/01.mp3","What can I get for you?\" asked the young man at the counter.":"materials/g05/02.mp3","\"A small coffee, please,\" said Emma.":"materials/g05/03.mp3","\"Hot or iced?\"":"materials/g05/04.mp3","\"Hot, please.":"materials/g05/05.mp3","And could I have a piece of that cake?\"":"materials/g05/06.mp3","\"Of course.":"materials/g05/07.mp3","For here or to go?\"":"materials/g05/08.mp3","\"For here.\"":"materials/g05/09.mp3","\"That will be six dollars.\"":"materials/g05/10.mp3","Emma paid with her card and sat by the window.":"materials/g05/11.mp3","The shop was warm and the music was soft.":"materials/g05/12.mp3","She opened her notebook and started to write a plan for her week.":"materials/g05/13.mp3","Coffee shops help her to think clearly.":"materials/g05/14.mp3","When she finished, she said \"Thank you\" to the young man and left with a smile.":"materials/g05/15.mp3"}},"g06":{"voice":"am_fenrir","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_fenrir（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"Tom wanted to learn the guitar.":"materials/g06/01.mp3","At first, he practiced for three hours every Sunday.":"materials/g06/02.mp3","But on Monday, he forgot most of it.":"materials/g06/03.mp3","He felt bad and almost stopped.":"materials/g06/04.mp3","Then his teacher gave him some advice: \"Play for twenty minutes every day.\"":"materials/g06/05.mp3","Tom did not believe it would work, but he tried it.":"materials/g06/06.mp3","After one month, he could play three songs.":"materials/g06/07.mp3","After three months, he played at his friend's party.":"materials/g06/08.mp3","Everyone was surprised.":"materials/g06/09.mp3","Tom learned an important thing.":"materials/g06/10.mp3","A little practice every day is better than a lot of practice once a week.":"materials/g06/11.mp3"}},"g07":{"voice":"af_heart","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_heart（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"Dear Mr. Lee, Thank you for your call yesterday.":"materials/g07/01.mp3","It was a pleasure to talk with you about your plans for the new shop.":"materials/g07/02.mp3","As we discussed, our company can design and build the shelves and counters you need.":"materials/g07/03.mp3","I have attached a simple plan and a price list. The total cost would be about twelve thousand dollars, and the work would take three weeks.":"materials/g07/04.mp3","If the plan looks good to you, we could meet next Tuesday or Wednesday to talk about the details.":"materials/g07/05.mp3","Please let me know which day is better for you.":"materials/g07/06.mp3","I look forward to working with you.":"materials/g07/07.mp3","Best regards, Anna Sato":"materials/g07/08.mp3"}},"g08":{"voice":"am_michael","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_michael（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"Every Monday at nine, our team has a short meeting.":"materials/g08/01.mp3","It only lasts fifteen minutes, and we all stand up.":"materials/g08/02.mp3","Our leader, David, asks three questions.":"materials/g08/03.mp3","What did you finish last week?":"materials/g08/04.mp3","What will you do this week?":"materials/g08/05.mp3","Is anything stopping your work?":"materials/g08/06.mp3","Each person answers in one or two minutes.":"materials/g08/07.mp3","If someone has a problem, we do not try to solve it in the meeting.":"materials/g08/08.mp3","Instead, two or three people talk about it later.":"materials/g08/09.mp3","At first, I thought the meeting was too short.":"materials/g08/10.mp3","But now I like it.":"materials/g08/11.mp3","Everyone knows what the others are doing, and we do not waste time.":"materials/g08/12.mp3"}},"g09":{"voice":"bf_emma","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bf_emma（イギリス英語・女性）","clips":{"Since last year, Yuki has worked from home three days a week.":"materials/g09/01.mp3","At first, she loved it.":"materials/g09/02.mp3","She did not need to take a crowded train, and she had more time for breakfast. But after a few months, she found some problems. She often worked late because there was no clear end to the day.":"materials/g09/03.mp3","She also felt lonely, because she could not chat with her co-workers.":"materials/g09/04.mp3","So Yuki made some rules for herself.":"materials/g09/05.mp3","She starts at nine and stops at six.":"materials/g09/06.mp3","She takes a walk at lunch.":"materials/g09/07.mp3","Once a week, she has a video call with a co-worker just to talk.":"materials/g09/08.mp3","Now she enjoys working from home again.":"materials/g09/09.mp3"}},"g10":{"voice":"bm_george","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bm_george（イギリス英語・男性）","clips":{"Next Friday, Leo has to give his first presentation in English.":"materials/g10/01.mp3","He will talk to a group of customers about a new product.":"materials/g10/02.mp3","He is worried, because his English is not perfect.":"materials/g10/03.mp3","His friend Maria gave him some useful tips.":"materials/g10/04.mp3","First, keep the slides simple, with only a few words on each one.":"materials/g10/05.mp3","Second, practice out loud many times, and record yourself.":"materials/g10/06.mp3","Third, speak slowly and pause after important points.":"materials/g10/07.mp3","Finally, it is fine to make small mistakes.":"materials/g10/08.mp3","People care more about the message than about perfect grammar.":"materials/g10/09.mp3","Leo feels a little better now.":"materials/g10/10.mp3","He has started to practice every evening.":"materials/g10/11.mp3"}},"g11":{"voice":"af_bella","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_bella（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"When I visited Taiwan last spring, my favorite place was a night market.":"materials/g11/01.mp3","It opened at six in the evening and stayed busy until midnight.":"materials/g11/02.mp3","There were hundreds of small stands selling food, clothes and toys.":"materials/g11/03.mp3","The air was full of smells: fried chicken, sweet potatoes, and a famous strong-smelling tofu.":"materials/g11/04.mp3","I was a little afraid of the tofu, but a friendly woman at the stand told me to try it.":"materials/g11/05.mp3","To my surprise, it was delicious.":"materials/g11/06.mp3","I also played a simple game and won a small toy.":"materials/g11/07.mp3","Walking through the bright, noisy market, I felt that I was really part of the city.":"materials/g11/08.mp3"}},"g12":{"voice":"am_fenrir","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_fenrir（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"Have you ever learned a new word and forgotten it the next day?":"materials/g12/01.mp3","This is very normal.":"materials/g12/02.mp3","More than a hundred years ago, a German scientist named Hermann Ebbinghaus studied memory.":"materials/g12/03.mp3","He found that we forget most new information within a day or two.":"materials/g12/04.mp3","But he also found good news.":"materials/g12/05.mp3","Each time we review the information, we forget it more slowly.":"materials/g12/06.mp3","So the best way to learn is to review new words several times, with longer and longer breaks between each review: after one day, then three days, then a week, and so on.":"materials/g12/07.mp3","Many language apps today use this simple idea.":"materials/g12/08.mp3"}},"w-internet":{"voice":"af_heart","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_heart（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"The Internet is the world’s largest global communication network for computers and other devices.":"materials/w-internet/01.mp3","It connects many smaller networks from homes, schools, businesses, and governments.":"materials/w-internet/02.mp3","These networks share different kinds of information.":"materials/w-internet/03.mp3","The short form of the Internet is “the Net.”":"materials/w-internet/04.mp3","One of its most popular services is the World Wide Web, which is used by billions of people every day.":"materials/w-internet/05.mp3","The Internet was developed in the United States by the Department of Defence Advanced Research Projects Agency (DARPA).":"materials/w-internet/06.mp3","The Internet was first connected in October 1969 and was called ARPANET.":"materials/w-internet/07.mp3","The World Wide Web was created at CERN in Switzerland in 1990 by a British (UK) scientist named Tim Berners-Lee.":"materials/w-internet/08.mp3"}},"w-elephant":{"voice":"am_michael","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_michael（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"Elephants are the biggest living land mammals.":"materials/w-elephant/01.mp3","They have long noses called trunks and large flapping ears.":"materials/w-elephant/02.mp3","The largest elephant ever recorded was shot in Angola in 1974.":"materials/w-elephant/03.mp3","It weighed 27,060 lb (12.27 t) and stood 13 ft 8 in (4.17 m) tall.":"materials/w-elephant/04.mp3","At birth, an elephant calf may be as big as 100 kg (225 pounds).":"materials/w-elephant/05.mp3","The baby elephant develops for 20 to 22 months inside its mother.":"materials/w-elephant/06.mp3","No other land animal takes this long to develop before being born.":"materials/w-elephant/07.mp3","In the wild, elephants have strong family relationships.":"materials/w-elephant/08.mp3","Their ways of acting toward other elephants are hard for people to understand.":"materials/w-elephant/09.mp3","They \"talk\" to each other with very low sounds.":"materials/w-elephant/10.mp3","Most elephants sounds are so low, people cannot hear them.":"materials/w-elephant/11.mp3","But elephants can hear these sounds from very far away.":"materials/w-elephant/12.mp3","Elephants have strong, leathery skin to protect themselves.":"materials/w-elephant/13.mp3"}},"w-bicycle":{"voice":"bf_emma","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bf_emma（イギリス英語・女性）","clips":{"A bicycle (or bike) is a small, human powered land vehicle with a seat, two wheels, two pedals, and a metal chain connected to cogs on the pedals and rear wheel.":"materials/w-bicycle/01.mp3","A frame gives the bike strength, and the other parts are attached to the frame.":"materials/w-bicycle/02.mp3","The name comes from the prefix bi (meaning two) and the suffix cycle (meaning wheel).":"materials/w-bicycle/03.mp3","It is powered by a person riding on top, who pushes the pedals around with his or her feet.":"materials/w-bicycle/04.mp3","Riding bicycles, which is also called cycling, is an important way to travel in several parts of the world.":"materials/w-bicycle/05.mp3","The most popular type of cycling is Utility cycling.":"materials/w-bicycle/06.mp3","It is also a common kind of recreation, a good form of low-impact exercise, and a popular sport.":"materials/w-bicycle/07.mp3","According to one study, road bicycle racing is the eighth most popular spectator sport in the world.":"materials/w-bicycle/08.mp3","Cycling uses less energy per mile than any other human transport.":"materials/w-bicycle/09.mp3"}},"w-coffee":{"voice":"bm_george","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bm_george（イギリス英語・男性）","clips":{"Coffee is a caffeinated drink prepared from roasted coffee beans.":"materials/w-coffee/01.mp3","It's also a plant (Coffea) and the name of the drink that is made from this plant.":"materials/w-coffee/02.mp3","The coffee plant is a bush or tree that can grow up to ten meters (about 32 feet) high, but is usually cut shorter.":"materials/w-coffee/03.mp3","Coffee plants originally grew in Ethiopia, and now also grow in South America, Central America, Southeast Asia and Turkey.":"materials/w-coffee/04.mp3","They are an important crop for the economies of many countries.":"materials/w-coffee/05.mp3","The drink is made from the seeds of the coffee plant, called coffee beans.":"materials/w-coffee/06.mp3","Coffee is usually served hot, and is a popular drink in many countries.":"materials/w-coffee/07.mp3","To make a drink from coffee beans, the beans must first be specially prepared by drying the beans and then roasting.":"materials/w-coffee/08.mp3","The beans are dried a short time after they are picked.":"materials/w-coffee/09.mp3","This preserves them and makes them ready to be packed or roasted.":"materials/w-coffee/10.mp3","Before the beans are made into a drink, they must be roasted and ground (crushed into tiny pieces in a coffee mill).":"materials/w-coffee/11.mp3","When the ground coffee is placed into boiling water, the flavour and dark brown colour of the beans goes into the water.":"materials/w-coffee/12.mp3","Making coffee is called brewing coffee.":"materials/w-coffee/13.mp3","There are several different ways that coffee can be brewed.":"materials/w-coffee/14.mp3"}},"w-olympics":{"voice":"af_bella","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_bella（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"The Olympic Games (French: Jeux olympiques) is an important international event featuring summer and winter sports.":"materials/w-olympics/01.mp3","Summer Olympic Games and Winter Olympic Games are held every four years.":"materials/w-olympics/02.mp3","Originally, the ancient Olympic Games were held in Ancient Greece at Olympia.":"materials/w-olympics/03.mp3","The first games were in 776 BC.":"materials/w-olympics/04.mp3","They were held every four years until the 6th century AC.":"materials/w-olympics/05.mp3","The first \"modern\" Olympics took place in 1896 in Athens, Greece.":"materials/w-olympics/06.mp3","Athletes participate in the Olympics Games to represent their countries.":"materials/w-olympics/07.mp3","Over time the Olympics have become bigger.":"materials/w-olympics/08.mp3","In old times, women were not allowed, but now there are women's events.":"materials/w-olympics/09.mp3","The Winter Games were created for ice and snow sports.":"materials/w-olympics/10.mp3","The Paralympic Games were created for athletes with physical disabilities.":"materials/w-olympics/11.mp3","As well, the Olympics became bigger with the addition of the Youth Olympic Games for teenage athletes.":"materials/w-olympics/12.mp3","World War I and World War II led to the cancellation of the 1916, 1940, and 1944 Games.":"materials/w-olympics/13.mp3","As the decision-making body, the International Olympic Committee (IOC) is responsible for choosing the host city for each Olympic Games.":"materials/w-olympics/14.mp3","The IOC is also responsible for choosing what sports are in the games.":"materials/w-olympics/15.mp3","The creator of modern Olympics is Baron Pierre de Coubertin.":"materials/w-olympics/16.mp3"}},"w-telephone":{"voice":"am_fenrir","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_fenrir（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"A telephone, also known as a phone, is a communication tool.":"materials/w-telephone/01.mp3","People use it to talk with people far away.":"materials/w-telephone/02.mp3","Originally, it was an electric tool sending analogue speech through wires.":"materials/w-telephone/03.mp3","Many telephones in the 21st century are electronic tools sending digital signals on wires or radio transmission.":"materials/w-telephone/04.mp3","Using a telephone, two people who are in different places can talk to each other.":"materials/w-telephone/05.mp3","Early telephones needed to be connected with wires which are called fixed or landline telephones.":"materials/w-telephone/06.mp3","Modern mobile phones use radio waves.":"materials/w-telephone/07.mp3"}},"w-chocolate":{"voice":"af_heart","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_heart（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"Chocolate is a food made from cacao beans.":"materials/w-chocolate/01.mp3","It is used in many desserts like pudding, cakes, candy, ice cream, and Easter eggs.":"materials/w-chocolate/02.mp3","It can be in a solid form like a candy bar or it can be in a liquid form like hot chocolate.":"materials/w-chocolate/03.mp3","Commercial chocolate has sugar and sometimes milk added.":"materials/w-chocolate/04.mp3","It has a melting point of about 30 to 32 °C (86 to 90 °F).":"materials/w-chocolate/05.mp3","Dark chocolate has less sugar, and a more bitter taste.":"materials/w-chocolate/06.mp3","It was originally used to make drinking chocolate.":"materials/w-chocolate/07.mp3","Chocolate has been around the world since the time of the Olmec, Mayan, and Aztecs.":"materials/w-chocolate/08.mp3"}},"w-fuji":{"voice":"am_michael","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_michael（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"Mount Fuji (富士山, Fuji-san) is the tallest mountain in Japan, at 3,776 metres (12,388 ft) high.":"materials/w-fuji/01.mp3","It is also a volcano. It is on the border between Shizuoka Prefecture and Yamanashi Prefecture.":"materials/w-fuji/02.mp3","Mount Fuji is a famous cultural icon of Japan, as a lot of people have painted it and taken photographs of it.":"materials/w-fuji/03.mp3","It became the 13th UNESCO World Heritage Site in Japan on June 22, 2013.":"materials/w-fuji/04.mp3","The last time it erupted was from 1707 to 1708.":"materials/w-fuji/05.mp3"}},"w-moon":{"voice":"bf_emma","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bf_emma（イギリス英語・女性）","clips":{"The Moon, also known as Luna, is Earth's only natural satellite (the only object which orbits the Earth and is not man-made).":"materials/w-moon/01.mp3","It is usually visible in the night sky, but is sometimes seen during the day.":"materials/w-moon/02.mp3","The Moon is about one-fourth of the width of Earth.":"materials/w-moon/03.mp3","Because it is so far away it looks small in the sky, about half a degree wide.":"materials/w-moon/04.mp3","The gravity on the Moon is one-sixth of the Earth's gravity.":"materials/w-moon/05.mp3","It means that an object will be one-sixth as heavy on the Moon compared to Earth.":"materials/w-moon/06.mp3","The Moon is a rocky and dusty place.":"materials/w-moon/07.mp3","It moves slowly away from the Earth at a rate of 3.8 centimeters per year due to the effect of tidal dissipation.":"materials/w-moon/08.mp3","Some other planets also have moons or natural satellites.":"materials/w-moon/09.mp3","The giant impact hypothesis is a common explanation for how the Moon formed.":"materials/w-moon/10.mp3"}},"w-email":{"voice":"bm_george","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bm_george（イギリス英語・男性）","clips":{"Electronic mail (or e-mail or email) is an Internet service that allows people who have an e-mail address (accounts) to send and receive electronic letters.":"materials/w-email/01.mp3","Those are much like postal letters, except that they are delivered much faster than snail mail when sending over long distances, and are usually free.":"materials/w-email/02.mp3","Like with regular mail, users may get a lot of unwanted mail.":"materials/w-email/03.mp3","With e-mail, this is called spam.":"materials/w-email/04.mp3","Some programs used for sending and receiving mail can detect spam and filter it out nearly completely.":"materials/w-email/05.mp3"}},"w-sleep":{"voice":"af_bella","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_bella（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"Sleep (also called napping) is a state of resting.":"materials/w-sleep/01.mp3","It happens in most animals, including humans.":"materials/w-sleep/02.mp3","To sleep is to be unconscious.":"materials/w-sleep/03.mp3","During deep sleep, most of the muscles that animals can control are not active, but resting to regain the energy they need for the next time they wake up.":"materials/w-sleep/04.mp3","When asleep, humans cannot tell what is happening around them.":"materials/w-sleep/05.mp3","Like most animals, healthy sleep in humans most often happens at night.":"materials/w-sleep/06.mp3","When something is asleep, it cannot react like it would if it was awake.":"materials/w-sleep/07.mp3","However, waking up from sleep is easier than waking up from hibernation or a coma.":"materials/w-sleep/08.mp3","All mammals and birds, as well as many reptiles, amphibians and fish have a sleep cycle.":"materials/w-sleep/09.mp3","In humans and many other animals, regular sleep is essential for survival.":"materials/w-sleep/10.mp3"}},"a-town-mouse":{"voice":"am_fenrir","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_fenrir（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"A Town Mouse once visited a relative who lived in the country.":"materials/a-town-mouse/01.mp3","For lunch the Country Mouse served wheat stalks, roots, and acorns, with a dash of cold water for drink.":"materials/a-town-mouse/02.mp3","The Town Mouse ate very sparingly, nibbling a little of this and a little of that, and by her manner making it very plain that she ate the simple food only to be polite.":"materials/a-town-mouse/03.mp3","After the meal the friends had a long talk, or rather the Town Mouse talked about her life in the city while the Country Mouse listened.":"materials/a-town-mouse/04.mp3","They then went to bed in a cozy nest in the hedgerow and slept in quiet and comfort until morning.":"materials/a-town-mouse/05.mp3","In her sleep the Country Mouse dreamed she was a Town Mouse with all the luxuries and delights of city life that her friend had described for her.":"materials/a-town-mouse/06.mp3","So the next day when the Town Mouse asked the Country Mouse to go home with her to the city, she gladly said yes.":"materials/a-town-mouse/07.mp3","When they reached the mansion in which the Town Mouse lived, they found on the table in the dining room the leavings of a very fine banquet.":"materials/a-town-mouse/08.mp3","There were sweetmeats and jellies, pastries, delicious cheeses, indeed, the most tempting foods that a Mouse can imagine.":"materials/a-town-mouse/09.mp3","But just as the Country Mouse was about to nibble a dainty bit of pastry, she heard a Cat mew loudly and scratch at the door.":"materials/a-town-mouse/10.mp3","In great fear the Mice scurried to a hiding place, where they lay quite still for a long time, hardly daring to breathe.":"materials/a-town-mouse/11.mp3","When at last they ventured back to the feast, the door opened suddenly and in came the servants to clear the table, followed by the House Dog.":"materials/a-town-mouse/12.mp3","The Country Mouse stopped in the Town Mouse's den only long enough to pick up her carpet bag and umbrella.":"materials/a-town-mouse/13.mp3","\"You may have luxuries and dainties that I have not,\" she said as she hurried away, \"but I prefer my plain food and simple life in the country with the peace and security that go with it.\"":"materials/a-town-mouse/14.mp3","Moral: Poverty with security is better than plenty in the midst of fear and uncertainty.":"materials/a-town-mouse/15.mp3"}},"a-fox-grapes":{"voice":"af_heart","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_heart（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"A Fox one day spied a beautiful bunch of ripe grapes hanging from a vine trained along the branches of a tree.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/01.mp3","The grapes seemed ready to burst with juice, and the Fox's mouth watered as he gazed longingly at them.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/02.mp3","The bunch hung from a high branch, and the Fox had to jump for it.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/03.mp3","The first time he jumped he missed it by a long way.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/04.mp3","So he walked off a short distance and took a running leap at it, only to fall short once more.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/05.mp3","Again and again he tried, but in vain.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/06.mp3","Now he sat down and looked at the grapes in disgust.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/07.mp3","\"What a fool I am,\" he said.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/08.mp3","\"Here I am wearing myself out to get a bunch of sour grapes that are not worth gaping for.\"":"materials/a-fox-grapes/09.mp3","And off he walked very, very scornfully.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/10.mp3","Moral: There are many who pretend to despise and belittle that which is beyond their reach.":"materials/a-fox-grapes/11.mp3"}},"a-lion-mouse":{"voice":"am_michael","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_michael（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"A Lion lay asleep in the forest, his great head resting on his paws.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/01.mp3","A timid little Mouse came upon him unexpectedly, and in her fright and haste to get away, ran across the Lion's nose.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/02.mp3","Roused from his nap, the Lion laid his huge paw angrily on the tiny creature to kill her.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/03.mp3","\"Spare me!\" begged the poor Mouse.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/04.mp3","\"Please let me go and some day I will surely repay you.\"":"materials/a-lion-mouse/05.mp3","The Lion was much amused to think that a Mouse could ever help him.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/06.mp3","But he was generous and finally let the Mouse go.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/07.mp3","Some days later, while stalking his prey in the forest, the Lion was caught in the toils of a hunter's net.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/08.mp3","Unable to free himself, he filled the forest with his angry roaring.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/09.mp3","The Mouse knew the voice and quickly found the Lion struggling in the net.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/10.mp3","Running to one of the great ropes that bound him, she gnawed it until it parted, and soon the Lion was free.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/11.mp3","\"You laughed when I said I would repay you,\" said the Mouse.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/12.mp3","\"Now you see that even a Mouse can help a Lion.\"":"materials/a-lion-mouse/13.mp3","Moral: A kindness is never wasted.":"materials/a-lion-mouse/14.mp3"}},"a-crow-pitcher":{"voice":"bf_emma","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bf_emma（イギリス英語・女性）","clips":{"In a spell of dry weather, when the Birds could find very little to drink, a thirsty Crow found a pitcher with a little water in it.":"materials/a-crow-pitcher/01.mp3","But the pitcher was high and had a narrow neck, and no matter how he tried, the Crow could not reach the water.":"materials/a-crow-pitcher/02.mp3","The poor thing felt as if he must die of thirst.":"materials/a-crow-pitcher/03.mp3","Then an idea came to him.":"materials/a-crow-pitcher/04.mp3","Picking up some small pebbles, he dropped them into the pitcher one by one.":"materials/a-crow-pitcher/05.mp3","With each pebble the water rose a little higher until at last it was near enough so he could drink.":"materials/a-crow-pitcher/06.mp3","Moral: In a pinch a good use of our wits may help us out.":"materials/a-crow-pitcher/07.mp3"}},"a-hare-tortoise":{"voice":"bm_george","voiceLabel":"Kokoro bm_george（イギリス英語・男性）","clips":{"A Hare was making fun of the Tortoise one day for being so slow.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/01.mp3","\"Do you ever get anywhere?\" he asked with a mocking laugh.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/02.mp3","\"Yes,\" replied the Tortoise, \"and I get there sooner than you think.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/03.mp3","I'll run you a race and prove it.\"":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/04.mp3","The Hare was much amused at the idea of running a race with the Tortoise, but for the fun of the thing he agreed.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/05.mp3","So the Fox, who had consented to act as judge, marked the distance and started the runners off.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/06.mp3","The Hare was soon far out of sight, and to make the Tortoise feel very deeply how ridiculous it was for him to try a race with a Hare, he lay down beside the course to take a nap until the Tortoise should catch up.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/07.mp3","The Tortoise meanwhile kept going slowly but steadily, and, after a time, passed the place where the Hare was sleeping.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/08.mp3","But the Hare slept on very peacefully; and when at last he did wake up, the Tortoise was near the goal.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/09.mp3","The Hare now ran his swiftest, but he could not overtake the Tortoise in time.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/10.mp3","Moral: The race is not always to the swift.":"materials/a-hare-tortoise/11.mp3"}},"a-wind-sun":{"voice":"af_bella","voiceLabel":"Kokoro af_bella（アメリカ英語・女性）","clips":{"The North Wind and the Sun had a quarrel about which of them was the stronger.":"materials/a-wind-sun/01.mp3","While they were disputing with much heat and bluster, a Traveler passed along the road wrapped in a cloak.":"materials/a-wind-sun/02.mp3","\"Let us agree,\" said the Sun, \"that he is the stronger who can strip that Traveler of his cloak.\"":"materials/a-wind-sun/03.mp3","\"Very well,\" growled the North Wind, and at once sent a cold, howling blast against the Traveler.":"materials/a-wind-sun/04.mp3","With the first gust of wind the ends of the cloak whipped about the Traveler's body.":"materials/a-wind-sun/05.mp3","But he immediately wrapped it closely around him, and the harder the Wind blew, the tighter he held it to him.":"materials/a-wind-sun/06.mp3","The North Wind tore angrily at the cloak, but all his efforts were in vain.":"materials/a-wind-sun/07.mp3","Then the Sun began to shine.":"materials/a-wind-sun/08.mp3","At first his beams were gentle, and in the pleasant warmth after the bitter cold of the North Wind, the Traveler unfastened his cloak and let it hang loosely from his shoulders.":"materials/a-wind-sun/09.mp3","The Sun's rays grew warmer and warmer.":"materials/a-wind-sun/10.mp3","The man took off his cap and mopped his brow.":"materials/a-wind-sun/11.mp3","At last he became so heated that he pulled off his cloak, and, to escape the blazing sunshine, threw himself down in the welcome shade of a tree by the roadside.":"materials/a-wind-sun/12.mp3","Moral: Gentleness and kind persuasion win where force and bluster fail.":"materials/a-wind-sun/13.mp3"}},"a-shepherd-boy":{"voice":"am_fenrir","voiceLabel":"Kokoro am_fenrir（アメリカ英語・男性）","clips":{"A Shepherd Boy tended his master's Sheep near a dark forest not far from the village.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/01.mp3","Soon he found life in the pasture very dull.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/02.mp3","All he could do to amuse himself was to talk to his dog or play on his shepherd's pipe.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/03.mp3","One day as he sat watching the Sheep and the quiet forest, and thinking what he would do should he see a Wolf, he thought of a plan to amuse himself.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/04.mp3","His Master had told him to call for help should a Wolf attack the flock, and the Villagers would drive it away.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/05.mp3","So now, though he had not seen anything that even looked like a Wolf, he ran toward the village shouting at the top of his voice, \"Wolf!":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/06.mp3","Wolf!\"":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/15.mp3","As he expected, the Villagers who heard the cry dropped their work and ran in great excitement to the pasture.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/08.mp3","But when they got there they found the Boy doubled up with laughter at the trick he had played on them.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/09.mp3","A few days later the Shepherd Boy again shouted, \"Wolf!":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/10.mp3","Again the Villagers ran to help him, only to be laughed at again.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/12.mp3","Then one evening as the sun was setting behind the forest and the shadows were creeping out over the pasture, a Wolf really did spring from the underbrush and fall upon the Sheep.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/13.mp3","In terror the Boy ran toward the village shouting \"Wolf!":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/14.mp3","But though the Villagers heard the cry, they did not run to help him as they had before.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/16.mp3","\"He cannot fool us again,\" they said.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/17.mp3","The Wolf killed a great many of the Boy's sheep and then slipped away into the forest.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/18.mp3","Moral: Liars are not believed even when they speak the truth.":"materials/a-shepherd-boy/19.mp3"}}}}